kinetic-energy-is-zero.conceptual_definition:
The formula "Kinetic energy is zero" (
 $k = 0$
) signifies a state where an object or system possesses no energy of motion. Kinetic energy, by definition, is the energy an object has due to its movement. Therefore, when kinetic energy is zero, the object is at rest, meaning its velocity is zero relative to the chosen frame of reference.
